      "id": "T1",
      "name": "Exact 2^L-Fold Cyclic Convolution and Harmonic Power Law",
      "statement": "Under a depth-L binary CNOT tree-merge aligning K = 2^L noisy DCP leaves on Z_q with i.i.d. symmetric phase error kernel K_eta, the post-selected root phase error follows the 2^L-fold cyclic convolution K_eta^(*2^L), and its m-th Fourier harmonic visibility equals Lambda_m^(L) = (lambda_m)^(2^L) exactly."
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "name": "Double-Exponential Root Visibility Decay and Per-Leaf Noise Threshold",
      "statement": "For any symmetric noise kernel with fundamental damping lambda_1 in (0, 1), the root visibility at tree depth L decays double-exponentially as Lambda_1^(L) = lambda_1^(2^L) = exp(-2^L ln(1/lambda_1)), requiring 1 - lambda_1 <= 1 - tau^(2^(-L)) to maintain root visibility >= tau."
    },
